<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghirlandina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Torre della Ghirlandina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ghirlandina is the bell tower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> Cathedral, about 87 metres tall, begun at the end of the 11th century and completed in its Gothic upper stages in the early 14th century. A civic symbol of Modena, it is part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> with the cathedral and the Piazza Grande.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghirlandina.jpg" alt="Ghirlandina" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FrDr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modena_0100_06-edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
